izing data to increase efficiency and visibility.Documenting the solutions developed and supporting end users during adoption.Collaborating with different stakeholders to understand their needs and translate them into technical solutions.Your Skills & ExperiencesCurrently pursuing aMaster’s/ Engineer degree in Data Science, Computer Science, Engineering, Business Intelligence, or a related field.Basic knowledge or first experience with Power BI, Power Apps, and/or Power Automate (training will be provided).Strong analytical mindset and solid data manipulation skills.Good command of Excel and the Microsoft Office suite.Ability to work independently and show initiative.Professional proficiency in English.What We OfferA hands-on internship with real impact on digital transformation initiatives.Mentorship and learning opportunities in data visualization and process automation.Exposure to Microsoft’s Power Platform ecosystem in a real business environment.A collaborative and supportive team._________________________________________________________________________ST is proud to be one of the 17 companies certified as a 2025 Global Top Employer and the first and only semiconductor company to achieve this distinction. ST was recognized in this ranking thanks to its continuous improvement approach and stands out particularly in the areas of ethics & integrity, purpose & values, organization & change, business strategy, and performance.At ST, we endeavor to foster a diverse and inclusive workplace, and we do not tolerate discrimination. We aim to recruit and retain a diverse workforce that reflects the societies around us. We strive for equity in career development, career opportunities, and equal remuneration. We encourage candidates who may not meet every single requirement to apply, as we appreciate diverse perspectives and provide opportunities for growth and learning. Diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI) is woven into our company culture.To discover more, visit st.com/