forts to improve model performance.Analyze retail and supply chain data to identify trends, anomalies, and business insights.Work with customer stakeholders and internal teams to improve forecast quality and replenishment effectiveness.Support continuous improvement initiatives related to forecasting models and business processes.Technical Support & AutomationUse Python and related tools to perform data analysis, automation, and model monitoring activities.Work with Docker, GitHub, and related development tools to support code management and deployments.Support issue resolution, troubleshooting, and validation of forecast outputs.Collaborate with engineering and product teams to address technical issues and implement improvements.Customer Engagement & ReportingParticipate in customer meetings to review forecast performance and discuss ongoing improvements.Prepare reports, dashboards, and summaries related to forecast accuracy and business performance.Maintain documentation related to forecasting logic, model assumptions, and process updates.Support ongoing customer production support activities and service delivery requirements.QualificationsBachelor’s degree in Data Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Engineering, Supply Chain, Computer Science, or a related field.1-3 years of experience in demand forecasting, data science, supply chain analytics, or retail planning.Basic understanding of demand planning, replenishment, and forecast accuracy measurement.Hands-on experience with Python, Pandas, and data analysis techniques.Familiarity with Docker, GitHub, and model deployment or support processes.Exposure to machine learning concepts and forecasting algorithms.Strong analytical, problem-solving, and troubleshooting skills.Ability to work in a customer-facing environment and collaborate effectively with multiple stakeholders.Strong communication and presentation skills.Preferred QualificationsFamiliarity with Polars and other modern data processing frameworks.Exposure to retail demand forecasting and replenishment systems.Experience working in managed services or production support environments.Knowledge of supply chain planning concepts and inventory optimization.French language proficiency would be an advantage.About UsWhat We OfferCompetitive salary and benefits package.Opportunity to work on high-impact retail forecasting and supply chain programs.Exposure to leading global retailers and advanced AI-driven planning solutions.A collaborative and fast-paced work environment.Learning and growth opportunities across retail, supply chain, and data science domains.", "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/search/?currentJobId=4409852800&keywords=data%20analyst%20Morocco&location=Morocco&start=25"}
