{"title": "Stagiaire PFE Eleve Ingenieur Data sciences / Power BI... ref 11217", "company": "STMicroelectronics", "location": "Bouskoura, Casablanca-Settat, Maroc·Republiéeil y a 4 jours·Plus de 100 personnes ont cliqué sur PostulerPromue par un recruteur·Réponses gérées en dehors de LinkedIn", "description": "À propos de l’offre d’emploiOUR STORYAt STMicroelectronics, we believe in the power of technology to drive innovation and make a positive impact on people, businesses, and society. As a global semiconductor company, our advanced technologies and chips form the hidden foundation of the world we live in today.When you join ST, you will be part of a global business with more than 115 nationalities, present in 40 countries, and comprising over 50,000 diverse and dedicated creators and makers of technology around the world.Developing technologies takes more than talent: it takes amazing people who understand collaboration and respect. People with passion and the desire to disrupt the status quo, drive innovation, and unlock their own potential.Embark on a journey with us, where you can innovate for a future that we want to make smarter and greener, in a responsible and sustainable way. Our technology starts with you._________________________________________________________________________________Internship Opportunity – Power BI & Automation InternYOUR ROLEAs a Power BI & Automation Intern, you will contribute to improving our digital tools and reporting capabilities within the team. Your mission will focus on creating, enhancing, and automating dashboards and workflows to help us optimize our internal processes.Your Responsibilities Will IncludeDesigning, building, and maintaining Power BI dashboards to support data-driven decision making.Developing simple automation solutions using Power Apps, Power Automate, and other Microsoft 365 tools.Analyzing existing manual processes and proposing digital automation alternatives.Assisting the team in structuring and visualizing data to increase efficiency and visibility.Documenting the solutions developed and supporting end users during adoption.Collaborating with different stakeholders to understand their needs and translate them into technical solutions.Your Skills & ExperiencesCurrently pursuing aMaster’s/ Engineer degree in Data Science, Computer Science, Engineering, Business Intelligence, or a related field.Basic knowledge or first experience with Power BI, Power Apps, and/or Power Automate (training will be provided).Strong analytical mindset and solid data manipulation skills.Good command of Excel and the Microsoft Office suite.Ability to work independently and show initiative.Professional proficiency in English.What We OfferA hands-on internship with real impact on digital transformation initiatives.Mentorship and learning opportunities in data visualization and process automation.Exposure to Microsoft’s Power Platform ecosystem in a real business environment.A collaborative and supportive team._________________________________________________________________________ST is proud to be one of the 17 companies certified as a 2025 Global Top Employer and the first and only semiconductor company to achieve this distinction. ST was recognized in this ranking thanks to its continuous improvement approach and stands out particularly in the areas of ethics & integrity, purpose & values, organization & change, business strategy, and performance.At ST, we endeavor to foster a diverse and inclusive workplace, and we do not tolerate discrimination. We aim to recruit and retain a diverse workforce that reflects the societies around us. We strive for equity in career development, career opportunities, and equal remuneration. We encourage candidates who may not meet every single requirement to apply, as we appreciate diverse perspectives and provide opportunities for growth and learning. Diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI) is woven into our company culture.To discover more, visit st.com/careers.", "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/search/?currentJobId=4400547220&keywords=stagiaire%20data%20Maroc&location=Morocco&start=25"}
{"title": "Data & AI Engineering Team Leader", "company": "AXA Global Business Services (AXA GBS)", "location": "Rabat, Rabat-Salé-Kénitra, Maroc·il y a 1 semaine·Plus de 100 candidatsPromue par un recruteur·Évaluation des candidatures en cours", "description": "À propos de l’offre d’emploiAXA Global Business Services Moroccois a subsidiary of AXA Group, one of the leading insurance brands in the world. We embody the essence of a diverse, global team, uniting talents from around the world to create a seamless, supportive network for all AXA entities. Our story is one of collaboration and growth, deeply rooted in our mission and vision, guiding every step we take.Our Mission:Together with entities, we deliver advanced services and shape solutions that drive operational excellence.In the heart of AXA, our role is multi-layered. From insurance operations to corporate functions, we leverage data, technology, and diverse capabilities to enhance our partners' performance in a streamlined, efficient manner.Our Vision:Building on unique capabilities and expertise, our teams dare to open new doors for AXA.We are not just about today; we are shaping tomorrow. Our vision is to continuously develop new skills and solutions, opening doors to fresh opportunities. This means committing to the highest service and quality levels, embracing continuous improvement, and fostering courage and boldness within our team.For over 25 years, our operations have spanned across five delivery centres in India and Morocco, serving more than 35 AXA entities. Our 3,800+ strong workforce is the heartbeat of our organisation, moving forward in a culture of trust, empowerment, and care. Driven by our values, we are a cohesive global team, quick to adapt to market dynamics, united by the desire to excel.Our Centres of Excellence (COEs) offer advanced services, shaping tailor-made solutions for our partners in the Tech, Security, Data, Insurance Ops and Corporate function Ops domain.The AXAllence strate